# TEMP SHIM README — wibwob-vps-smoke

Status: **temporary compatibility shim**
Date: 2026-03-18
Owner intent: consolidate smoke skills under one canonical path while avoiding prompt/runbook breakage.

## Why this exists

Two skill dirs currently exist:

- Canonical: `.pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke`
- Legacy: `.pi/skills/wibwob-vps-smoke`

`wibwob-hosting-smoke` is the semantic superset (docker-vps, flyio, npm-global adapters).
`wibwob-vps-smoke` is kept only to avoid breaking older prompts and docs while migration completes.

## What changed in this shim

- `SKILL.md` now marks this skill as deprecated.
- `scripts/run-smoke.sh` now delegates to:
  - `bash .pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/scripts/run-smoke.sh docker-vps`
- `scripts/summarize-latest-smoke.py` now delegates to hosting-smoke summarizer.

This directory should no longer gain new feature logic.

## Canonical usage (from now on)

```bash
bash .pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/scripts/run-smoke.sh docker-vps
bash .pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/scripts/run-smoke.sh flyio
bash .pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/scripts/run-smoke.sh npm-global
python3 .pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/scripts/summarize-latest-smoke.py
```

## Artifact policy

- Runtime smoke artifacts: `scratch/captures/*`
- Curated durable evidence: `.pi/skills/wibwob-hosting-smoke/references/evidence/*` (if needed)
- **Do not write new transient files** into `.pi/skills/wibwob-vps-smoke/outpts`

## Consolidation plan

### Phase 1 (now) — canonical flip + deprecation
- [x] Mark legacy skill deprecated
- [x] Delegate legacy runners to hosting-smoke
- [x] Add this README shim note

### Phase 2 — artifact path normalization
- [ ] Move/curate useful legacy `outpts/*` evidence
- [ ] Keep transient evidence in `scratch/captures/*`

### Phase 3 — reference migration + guardrails
- [ ] Replace active doc references to `wibwob-vps-smoke` with `wibwob-hosting-smoke`
- [ ] Add guardrail check to catch new writes to legacy `outpts`

### Phase 4 — shim retirement
Retire this directory after:
- [ ] no active runbooks depend on it
- [ ] two stable smoke cycles use hosting-smoke only
- [ ] no unresolved operator confusion in devlog

## Non-goals in shim

- no new checks
- no adapter logic additions
- no duplicate eval model evolution

All of that belongs in `wibwob-hosting-smoke`.
